  "description": "Design a social news feed (Flipkart's console round, Uber's ranking follow-up): posts, follows, votes and comments, pull and push feed generators, rankers and cursor pagination, in Java, Python and C++14.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">Read 55 min</span><span class=\"chip\">Build 90 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Machine-coding case study</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Rank 19 of 45</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Social Network &amp; News Feed</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Users follow users, post, comment and vote; each user sees a feed. We build it as Flipkart asks it (a console app with a ranking rule) and as Uber and Microsoft ask it (running code, then \"let each user choose how the feed is ranked\"). You will learn the two strategies every feed is built on, pull (merge at read time) and push (fan out at write time), why they are a Strategy and an Observer, and how to paginate without losing posts.</p>\n"
  },
